<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhadradri Kothagudem district</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhadradri Kothagudem district is a district in the north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telangana">Telangana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, created in 2016 from part of the former Khammam district. Its headquarters is Kothagudem, and it includes the temple town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhadrachalam">Bhadrachalam</a> and the industrial town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palvancha">Palvancha</a>. Crossed by the Godavari, it is heavily forested and rich in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a>, mined by the Singareni Collieries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhadradri-kothagudem-district.jpg" alt="Bhadradri Kothagudem district" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adityamadhav83 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_View_of_Bhadrachalam_Gopuram.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
